==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/t͡ʃɛkt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-checked.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-checked.wav|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛkt|s=1}}

===Adjective===
{{head|en|adjective}}

# Marked with a check mark.
#: {{syn|en|ticked}}
# {{lb|en|North America}} Having a pattern of [[checks]]; [[checkered]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''checked''' tie}}
# {{lb|en|phonology}} Of [[syllables]], having a [[coda]].
# {{lb|en|phonology}} Of [[consonants]], [[glottalized]].
# Verified or validated in some way.
#: {{ux|en|a computer program using '''checked''' arithmetic}}
# {{lb|en|aviation|_|or other|_|transport|of baggage}} Delivered to the [[airline]] (or [[train]] [[line]], [[ferry]], etc.), usually during [[check-in]], to be stored in an [[inaccessible]] area to the [[passenger]] (the [[hold#Noun|hold]]) during the [[flight]] (or other journey).
#: {{ant|en|carry-on}}
# {{lb|en|crosswording}} Of a letter square in a crossword grid, part of both an across word and a down word.

